      "output": "Jen Stevenson Zepeda serves as a Commercial Solar Consultant for ReVision Energy [1]. Johnna Flahive's research explores the impact of climate change initiatives on transient populations, such as seasonal workers and the homeless [2]. Her research includes a project investigating historical barriers to and future opportunities for transient populations in climate resilience policy and planning, as well as an NOAA-funded project regarding how these populations can participate in climate discourse as stakeholders [2]. Additionally, Flahive is developing a socio-ecological dynamic systems model to explore the relationship between flood environments and homeless populations [2]. She also conducts research, funded by the Sustainable Solutions Lab and the National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration\u2019s (NOAA) Adaptation Sciences (AdSci) program, that explores how coastal inundation impacts people living unhoused and seasonal workers in Massachusetts [3].",
